1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,760
Hey Skill enthusiasts, an essential open-source Skill manager is here! I'm sure we've all been there: after installing a bunch of Skills...

2
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:04,320
and have no idea where the Skill went.

3
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:05,680
And you end up installing a ton of them.

4
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:06,560
You want to manage them, but you just don't know how.

5
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:07,580
and have no idea how to manage them.

6
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:09,780
Even I myself have iterated on my Skills a lot.

7
00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:12,040
So, how do you handle version control for each and every Skill?

8
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:14,880
I've got a Skill on my Mac mini,

9
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:18,000
and the ones on my MacBook Air.

10
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,480
But that process is riddled with problems.

11
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:21,380
So, is it possible to build a Skill manager?

12
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:22,440
Based on Uncle Huang's own experience

13
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:25,080
and based on the needs of the many users in our community,

14
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:27,410
So, Uncle Huang has open-sourced this Skill manager.

15
00:00:27,410 --> 00:00:30,530
So, let's do a quick rundown of what this manager can do.

16
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:33,340
Alright, so first off, once we open it up...

17
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:35,040
It can perform a quick, one-click scan,

18
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:36,400
in less than a second.

19
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,660
It scans your entire computer and pulls up every single skill you have.

20
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:42,300
This includes both global and project-level skills.

21
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:43,460
And we can filter all of them.

22
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:45,940
Whether it's for Claude Code, or Cursor,

23
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:47,940
or Codex, or openclaw.

24
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:50,900
We can also sort them into different categories.

25
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:55,269
And for each Skill, we can take a detailed look at it.

26
00:00:55,269 --> 00:00:57,709
This includes keeping a version history for it.

27
00:00:57,709 --> 00:00:59,389
We can create a snapshot.

28
00:00:59,389 --> 00:01:03,560
So, it's basically like Git, handling version control for the entire Skill.

29
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:06,080
Alright, see? It's just taken a version snapshot right there.

30
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:07,840
So, if you run into a problem next time,

31
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:09,660
then you can just roll it back.

32
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:11,360
So, let's say you've installed a ton of skills.

33
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:12,720
and you want to streamline them,

34
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:15,420
You can click to select, or select multiple items at once.

35
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:18,340
And then, for example, let's say I don't want this one.

36
00:01:18,340 --> 00:01:23,720
So, you can select multiple ones, and then just click delete.

37
00:01:23,720 --> 00:01:26,300
So, when you delete something, it doesn't actually get removed permanently. Instead, it goes into the Recycle Bin.

38
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:27,870
and it will be kept there for seven days.

39
00:01:27,870 --> 00:01:30,390
for 7 days. So, you don't have to worry about accidentally deleting the wrong one.

40
00:01:30,390 --> 00:01:34,690
So, as you can see, these are some of the various skills I have in my Recycle Bin.

41
00:01:34,690 --> 00:01:35,970
If you want to delete it right away,

42
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:37,330
you can click 'Delete Permanently'.

43
00:01:37,330 --> 00:01:38,210
Or, you can just leave it be.

44
00:01:38,210 --> 00:01:38,850
After 7 days,

45
00:01:38,850 --> 00:01:42,749
it will automatically process all the skills in the Recycle Bin, and then...

46
00:01:42,749 --> 00:01:45,140
We also have a similarity detection feature.

47
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:48,780
Because you might have several similar skills installed at the same time.

48
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:51,120
So, in a situation like this, actually, CC...

49
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:53,520
and you're not sure which one to call.

50
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:55,740
So, to tackle this, we've built in a similarity detection feature.

51
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:56,980
And you'll be able to see, like,

52
00:01:56,980 --> 00:01:59,500
and see which Skills are closely related.

53
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:02,620
For example, these three are all related to email.

54
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:05,320
See? You can then take action on some of them.

55
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:06,920
And we've also included a dashboard in here.

56
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:08,160
This way, you can quickly see

57
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:12,380
and which modules your current Skills are being used in.

58
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:14,560
So you can see everything clearly and at a glance.

59
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:16,760
And on top of that, we've also built in a synchronization mechanism.

60
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:18,440
All you have to do is use a repository.

61
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:21,720
and you'll be able to upload your local Skills to it.

62
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:24,000
and then download them onto your other devices.

63
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,360
See, right here we can just click on 'Get Help'.

64
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,120
and download them from there.

65
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:31,100
As you can see, hey, there are various dimensions to it.

66
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:32,560
So we can take all of that into consideration.

67
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:36,220
So, which ones exactly do I need to download and save to my local machine?

68
00:02:36,220 --> 00:02:38,000
So, right here in our GitHub repository...

69
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:43,030
If we scroll down, you'll see that under 'Tools', there's something called Skillhub.

70
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:45,250
All you have to do is take this command line,

71
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:47,430
Then, open up any terminal window.

72
00:02:47,430 --> 00:02:48,510
and paste it in.

73
00:02:48,510 --> 00:02:50,550
and it'll automatically finish downloading.

74
00:02:50,550 --> 00:02:53,420
Then, go back to the browser window from earlier.

75
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:56,600
to help you scan your entire computer.

76
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:58,560
and perform a full system scan for your Skills.

77
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:00,430
to help you manage them more conveniently.

78
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:03,890
Of course, sometimes you might be thinking, 'Hey, what if I close this browser window?'

79
00:03:03,890 --> 00:03:04,890
But that's no problem.

80
00:03:04,890 --> 00:03:05,710
to start it up again.

81
00:03:05,710 --> 00:03:06,930
All you have to do is enter this command.

82
00:03:06,930 --> 00:03:09,670
Just type this command directly into your terminal.

83
00:03:09,670 --> 00:03:11,630
and it'll launch right up.

84
00:03:11,630 --> 00:03:14,750
So, this entire Skill manager is completely open-source.

85
00:03:14,750 --> 00:03:19,180
Feel free to check out my GitHub repository, and don't forget to give it a like or a fork.

86
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:21,060
Alright, that's all for today's content from your Uncle Huang.

87
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:22,820
See you in the next one.

